Available commands:

/start — start using the bot
➕ /add — add a place. Fill the fields in any order: use the buttons or just send a location, photo, venue, link or text. Only the name is required. You can also send a place link from Yandex Maps, Google Maps or 2GIS (“Share” → copy link): the bot fills in the name, address and location as far as it can.
📍 /places — your places: search, filters and sorting (including by rating), card, show on the map, edit, delete and publish to groups
🧭 /nearby — send a location and I will show your places nearby and places from your groups (marked 👥, can be turned off in /settings); the radius can be changed, and hints tell how many more places are in a larger radius
⚙️ /settings — language, default /nearby radius and auto-clean of service messages
🗑 /deleteme — download your data as a file or delete it from the bot completely
❓ /help — this help

⭐ *Ratings and comments.* In a place card you can rate it from 1 to 5 and leave a comment (one per place, editable) — everyone who has this place, or was shown it in a group or via a link, sees them; nobody sees the authors. If the same venue was saved as two different places, the "🔀 Different place" button merges them.

🔗 *Sharing.* In a place card press "🔗 Share" and send the link to a friend: they save the place for themselves (name, description and photo are copied; your later edits do not change theirs). You can limit the link to 1, 7 or 30 days or revoke it right there. You can also type `@bot_name place name` in any chat and pick one of your places: a card with a "Save for myself" button is sent straight to the chat.

👥 *Groups.* Places are added in a private chat only. To show a place to friends, open it in /places and press "📢 To groups" (or "Publish to groups" in the list to choose several). All places are private by default. In a group, /places (the group places) and /nearby (reply to the bot message with a location) work.